#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to create a parallel transpilation program and deploy it to IBM Quantum Platform to use as a reusable remote service."
msgstr "Paano gumawa ng parallel transpilation program at i-deploy ito sa IBM Quantum Platform para magamit bilang reusable remote service."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a Qiskit Function template for Hamiltonian simulation"
msgstr "Gumawa ng Qiskit Function template para sa Hamiltonian simulation"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/function-template-hamiltonian-simulation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/function-template-hamiltonian-simulation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This template encapsulates a workflow to simulate the time evolution of an initial state against a user defined spin-based Hamiltonian and returns a set of specified expectation values using the [AQC-Tensor](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) Qiskit addon.\n"
msgstr "Ang template na ito ay sumasaklaw sa isang workflow para sa pag-simulate ng time evolution ng isang initial state sa ilalim ng isang user-defined spin-based Hamiltonian at nagbabalik ng isang hanay ng mga tinukoy na expectation values gamit ang [AQC-Tensor](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) Qiskit addon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This template is structured as a Qiskit pattern with the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Ang template na ito ay nakabalangkas bilang isang Qiskit pattern na may mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Collecting input and mapping the problem {#1-collecting-input-and-mapping-the-problem}"
msgstr "1. Pangongolekta ng input at pag-map ng problema {#1-collecting-input-and-mapping-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section takes as an input the Hamiltonian to simulate, an initial state in the form of a `QuantumCircuit`, a set of observables to estimate expectation values, and a specification of options for the AQC addon. This step validates that all required input data is present and that they are in the correct format.\n"
msgstr "Ang seksyong ito ay tumatanggap bilang input ng Hamiltonian na isi-simulate, isang initial state sa anyo ng `QuantumCircuit`, isang hanay ng mga observable para sa pag-estimate ng expectation values, at isang pagtukoy ng mga opsyon para sa AQC addon. Bine-validate ng hakbang na ito na lahat ng kinakailangang input data ay naroroon at nasa tamang format.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The input arguments are then used to construct the relevant quantum circuits and operators for the workflow. A target circuit is created and a matrix product state representation of this circuit is found using the AQC addon. Following this, an ansatz circuit is generated and optimized using tensor network methods, producing a final circuit which executes the remainder of the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga input argument ay ginagamit pagkatapos upang buuin ang mga kaugnay na quantum circuit at operator para sa workflow. Isang target circuit ang nilikha at isang matrix product state representation ng circuit na ito ang natagpuan gamit ang AQC addon. Kasunod nito, isang ansatz circuit ang nalilikha at ino-optimize gamit ang tensor network methods, na nagpo-produce ng final circuit na nag-e-execute ng natitirang bahagi ng time evolution.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Prepare the generated circuits for execution {#2-prepare-the-generated-circuits-for-execution}"
msgstr "2. Paghahanda ng mga nabuong circuit para sa execution {#2-prepare-the-generated-circuits-for-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The generated circuits from the AQC addon are then transpiled to execute on a chosen backend. An [`EstimatorV2`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) instance is created with a default set of error mitigation options to manage the circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga nabuong circuit mula sa AQC addon ay ini-transpile para ma-execute sa isang piniling backend. Isang [`EstimatorV2`](../api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) instance ang nilikha na may default na hanay ng mga error mitigation option para pamahalaan ang circuit execution.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Execution {#3-execution}"
msgstr "3. Execution {#3-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the ansatz circuit is transpiled and executed on a QPU and collects estimates for all of the specified expectation values, which are returned in a serializable format for access by the user.\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, ang ansatz circuit ay ini-transpile at ine-execute sa isang QPU at nangongolekta ng mga estimate para sa lahat ng tinukoy na expectation values, na ibinabalik sa isang serializable na format para ma-access ng user.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the function template {#write-the-function-template}"
msgstr "Isulat ang function template {#write-the-function-template}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, write a function template for Hamiltonian simulation that uses the [AQC-Tensor Qiskit addon](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) to map the problem description to a reduced-depth circuit for execution on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Una, sumulat ng function template para sa Hamiltonian simulation na gumagamit ng [AQC-Tensor Qiskit addon](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-aqc-tensor/) para i-map ang paglalarawan ng problema sa isang reduced-depth circuit para sa execution sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you download this page and view it locally in a notebook editor, you will see some of the code cells contain the [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. This magic command saves the code to `./source_files/template_hamiltonian_simulation.py`, which is the function template you can upload to and run remotely with Qiskit Serverless.\n"
msgstr "Kung ida-download mo ang pahinang ito at titingnan nang lokal sa isang notebook editor, makikita mo na ang ilang code cell ay naglalaman ng [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) na `%%writefile`. Sine-save ng magic command na ito ang code sa `./source_files/template_hamiltonian_simulation.py`, na siyang function template na maaari mong i-upload at patakbuhin nang remote gamit ang Qiskit Serverless.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect and validate the inputs {#collect-and-validate-the-inputs}"
msgstr "Kolektahin at i-validate ang mga input {#collect-and-validate-the-inputs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start by getting the inputs for the template. This example has domain-specific inputs relevant for Hamiltonian simulation (such as the Hamiltonian and observable) and capability-specific options (such as how much you want to compress the initial layers of the Trotter circuit using AQC-Tensor, or advanced options for fine-tuning error suppression and mitigation beyond the defaults that are part of this example).\n"
msgstr "Magsimula sa pamamagitan ng pagkuha ng mga input para sa template. Ang halimbawang ito ay may mga domain-specific na input na may kaugnayan sa Hamiltonian simulation (tulad ng Hamiltonian at observable) at mga capability-specific na opsyon (tulad ng kung gaano kalaki ang gusto mong i-compress ang mga initial layer ng Trotter circuit gamit ang AQC-Tensor, o mga advanced na opsyon para sa fine-tuning ng error suppression at mitigation na lampas sa mga default na bahagi ng halimbawang ito).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the function template is running, it is helpful to return information in the logs by using print statements, so that you can better evaluate the workload's progress. Following is a simple example of printing the `estimator_options` so  there is a record of the actual Estimator options used. There are many more similar examples throughout the program to report progress during execution, including the value of the objective function during the iterative component of AQC-Tensor, and the two-qubit depth of the final instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit intended for execution on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Kapag tumatakbo ang function template, kapaki-pakinabang na magbalik ng impormasyon sa mga log sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga print statement, para mas madali mong masuri ang progreso ng workload. Narito ang isang simpleng halimbawa ng pag-print ng `estimator_options` para may rekord ang mga aktwal na Estimator option na ginamit. Marami pang katulad na halimbawa sa buong programa para mag-ulat ng progreso sa panahon ng execution, kabilang ang halaga ng objective function sa panahon ng iterative na bahagi ng AQC-Tensor, at ang two-qubit depth ng final instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit na nilayong i-execute sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate the inputs {#validate-the-inputs}"
msgstr "I-validate ang mga input {#validate-the-inputs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An important aspect of ensuring that the template can be reused across a range of inputs is input validation. The following code is an example of verifying that the stopping fidelity during AQC-Tensor has been specified appropriately and if not, returning an informative error message for how to fix the error.\n"
msgstr "Isang mahalagang aspeto ng pagtitiyak na ang template ay maaaring magamit muli sa iba't ibang input ay ang input validation. Ang sumusunod na code ay isang halimbawa ng pag-verify na ang stopping fidelity sa panahon ng AQC-Tensor ay naitakda nang tama at kung hindi, nagbababalik ng impormatibong mensahe ng error kung paano ayusin ang error.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the function outputs {#prepare-the-function-outputs}"
msgstr "Ihanda ang mga output ng function {#prepare-the-function-outputs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, prepare a dictionary to hold all of the function template outputs. Keys will be added to this dictionary throughout the workflow, and it is returned at the end of the program.\n"
msgstr "Una, maghanda ng dictionary para hawakan ang lahat ng output ng function template. Ang mga key ay idadagdag sa dictionary na ito sa buong workflow, at ibinabalik ito sa katapusan ng programa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map the problem and pre-process the circuit with AQC {#map-the-problem-and-pre-process-the-circuit-with-aqc}"
msgstr "I-map ang problema at i-pre-process ang circuit gamit ang AQC {#map-the-problem-and-pre-process-the-circuit-with-aqc}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AQC-Tensor optimization happens in step 1 of a Qiskit pattern.  First, a target state is constructed.  In this example, it is constructed from a target circuit that evolves the same Hamiltonian for the same time period as the AQC portion.  Then, an ansatz is generated from an equivalent circuit but with fewer Trotter steps.  In the main portion of the AQC algorithm, that ansatz is iteratively brought closer to the target state.  Finally, the result is combined with the remainder of the Trotter steps needed to reach the desired evolution time.\n"
msgstr "Ang AQC-Tensor optimization ay nagaganap sa hakbang 1 ng isang Qiskit pattern. Una, isang target state ang binubuo. Sa halimbawang ito, ito ay binubuo mula sa isang target circuit na nag-e-evolve ng parehong Hamiltonian para sa parehong tagal ng panahon tulad ng bahagi ng AQC. Pagkatapos, isang ansatz ang nalilikha mula sa isang katumbas na circuit ngunit na may mas kaunting mga Trotter step. Sa pangunahing bahagi ng AQC algorithm, ang ansatz na iyon ay paulit-ulit na inilalapit sa target state. Sa wakas, ang resulta ay pinagsama sa natitirang mga Trotter step na kailangan para maabot ang nais na evolution time.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note the additional examples of logging incorporated in the following code.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan ang mga karagdagang halimbawa ng logging na naka-incorporate sa sumusunod na code.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize the final circuit for execution {#optimize-the-final-circuit-for-execution}"
msgstr "I-optimize ang final circuit para sa execution {#optimize-the-final-circuit-for-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the AQC portion of the workflow, the `final_circuit` is [transpiled for the hardware](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) as usual.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ng bahagi ng AQC ng workflow, ang `final_circuit` ay [ini-transpile para sa hardware](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) tulad ng karaniwan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exit early if using dry run mode {#exit-early-if-using-dry-run-mode}"
msgstr "Lumabas nang maaga kung gumagamit ng dry run mode {#exit-early-if-using-dry-run-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If dry run mode has been selected, then the program is stopped before executing on hardware. This can be useful if, for example, you want first to inspect the two-qubit depth of the ISA circuit before deciding to execute on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Kung pinili ang dry run mode, ang programa ay titigil bago mag-execute sa hardware. Maaari itong maging kapaki-pakinabang kung, halimbawa, nais mo munang suriin ang two-qubit depth ng ISA circuit bago magpasya na mag-execute sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the circuit on hardware {#execute-the-circuit-on-hardware}"
msgstr "I-execute ang circuit sa hardware {#execute-the-circuit-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save the output {#save-the-output}"
msgstr "I-save ang output {#save-the-output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This function template returns the relevant domain-level output for this Hamiltonian simulation workflow (expectation values) in addition to important metadata generated along the way.\n"
msgstr "Ang function template na ito ay nagbabalik ng kaugnay na domain-level na output para sa Hamiltonian simulation workflow na ito (expectation values) kasama ang mahahalagang metadata na nabuong sa proseso.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deploy the function to IBM Quantum Platform {#deploy-the-function-to-ibm-quantum-platform}"
msgstr "I-deploy ang function sa IBM Quantum Platform {#deploy-the-function-to-ibm-quantum-platform}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous section created a program to be run remotely. The code in this section uploads that program to Qiskit Serverless.\n"
msgstr "Ginawa ng nakaraang seksyon ang isang program na tatakbo nang malayo. Ang code sa seksyong ito ay nag-a-upload ng program na iyon sa Qiskit Serverless.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `qiskit-ibm-catalog` to authenticate to `QiskitServerless` with your API key, which you can find on the [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) dashboard, and upload the program.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `qiskit-ibm-catalog` para mag-authenticate sa `QiskitServerless` gamit ang iyong API key, na makikita sa [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) dashboard, at i-upload ang program.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can optionally use `save_account()` to save your credentials (see the [Set up your IBM Cloud account](/guides/cloud-setup#cloud-save) guide). Note that this writes your credentials to the same file as [`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#save_account).\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang gumamit ng `save_account()` para i-save ang iyong mga kredensyal (tingnan ang gabay na [Set up your IBM Cloud account](/guides/cloud-setup#cloud-save)). Tandaan na isusulat nito ang iyong mga kredensyal sa parehong file tulad ng [`QiskitRuntimeService.save_account()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#save_account).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This program has custom `pip` dependencies.  Add them to a `dependencies` array when constructing the `QiskitFunction` instance:\n"
msgstr "Ang program na ito ay may custom na `pip` dependencies. Idagdag ang mga ito sa isang `dependencies` array kapag ginagawa ang `QiskitFunction` instance:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, check if the program successfully uploaded, use `serverless.list()`:\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, para suriin kung matagumpay na na-upload ang program, gamitin ang `serverless.list()`:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the function template remotely {#run-the-function-template-remotely}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang function template nang malayo {#run-the-function-template-remotely}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function template has been uploaded, so you can run it remotely with Qiskit Serverless. First, load the template by name:\n"
msgstr "Na-upload na ang function template, kaya maaari mo na itong patakbuhin nang malayo gamit ang Qiskit Serverless. Una, i-load ang template ayon sa pangalan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, run the template with the domain-level inputs for Hamiltonian simulation. This example specifies a 50-qubit XXZ model with random couplings, and an initial state and observable.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, patakbuhin ang template gamit ang mga domain-level na input para sa Hamiltonian simulation. Sa halimbawang ito, tinutukoy ang isang 50-qubit na XXZ model na may random na couplings, at isang initial state at observable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status of the job:\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang status ng job:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job is running, you can fetch logs created from the `print()` outputs. These can provide actionable information about the progress of the Hamiltonian simulation workflow. For example, the value of the objective function during the iterative component of AQC, or the two-qubit depth of the final ISA circuit intended for execution on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos na tumatakbo na ang job, maaari kang kumuha ng mga log na nagmula sa mga `print()` na output. Makapagbibigay ito ng impormasyong maaari mong pagbatayan ng aksyon tungkol sa progreso ng Hamiltonian simulation workflow. Halimbawa, ang halaga ng objective function sa panahon ng iterative na bahagi ng AQC, o ang two-qubit depth ng panghuling ISA circuit na nilalayon para sa execution sa hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Block the rest of the program until a result is available. After the job is done, you can retrieve the results. These include the domain-level output of Hamiltonian simulation (expectation value) and useful metadata.\n"
msgstr "I-block ang natitirang bahagi ng program hanggang may available na resulta. Pagkatapos matapos ang job, maaari mong makuha ang mga resulta. Kasama rito ang domain-level na output ng Hamiltonian simulation (expectation value) at mga kapaki-pakinabang na metadata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job completes, the entire logging output will be available.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos makumpleto ang job, ang buong logging output ay magiging available na.\n"

